rns were empty in about 45 months. They are not comparable to these.", "integration": {"decision": "No momentum variant reaches a weight. policy.MOMENTUM_VIEW stays None.", "reason": "Not one of nine variants clears |t| >= 3 on the Fama-MacBeth slope or on a long-only top-decile spread, on a panel where momentum should be at its strongest. The best conventional forms, volatility-scaled 12-1 and 6-1, reach rank-IC t of 2.3 and 2.2: suggestive, not established. The 52-week-high signal clears the bar on rank IC alone (t 3.45, rising with horizon) while its top-decile spread against the universe is about zero, so it ranks names without producing a spread a long-only tilt could harvest: within the top half of the ranking the IC is zero, and the whole effect sits among names far from their highs, which is George and Hwang's own finding and a short-side one. Conditioning value on momentum does not help: value's IC is higher among past losers than past winners. The mechanism to admit a view is built, tested and switched off; a variant that clears the bar on a future run enters with the IC it measured.", "established_elsewhere": "The value composite on this panel (book-to-market, earnings, free-cash-flow and EBIT yields) has IC 0.051 with t 3.86 over 164 months \u2014 the first cross-sectional signal in this repo established on a broad panel. Small caps; the book's own value score is untested until its sixth snapshot."}}